          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.5 Are Changes Permanent?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.135,
            0.882,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Once something has undergone a change, can we get it back in its original form?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.187,
            0.519,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 5.8: Let us think"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.221,
            0.883,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think again about all the changes that we have discussed or talked about so far. In which of these can we get back the object or substance in the form we started with? Record your observations in Table 5.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.338,
            0.877,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.265,
                0.306,
                0.628,
                0.328
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 5.2: Can changes be reversed?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.259,
                0.338,
                0.877,
                0.6
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_table_6.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>S.No.</td><td>Change</td><td rowspan=2>The original state can bebrought back (Yes/No)Yes</td></tr><tr><td>1.</td><td>Melting ice cubes</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Chopping vegetables</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Boiling water</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Making popcorn from corn</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>5.</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>12.</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.606,
            0.885,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Returning to the original object or substance with which we started shows that the changes we brought can be "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "reversed",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". For example, when ice melts, it can be refrozen into ice. Similarly, when water evaporates, it can be condensed back into liquid water. However, some changes cannot be reversed since we cannot get the original object or substance back after the change. For example, chopped vegetables cannot return to their original size and shape, and making popcorn cannot go back to its original form. Thus, changes around us could be grouped into those that can be reversed and those that cannot be reversed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.808,
            0.723,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.6 Are All Changes Desirable?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.855,
            0.885,
            0.932
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Many useful changes happen in our daily life. For example, the changing of milk into curd, ripening of fruits, cutting of fruits, and cooking of food. All these are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "desirable",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " changes. Can you think of some other desirable changes happening around you?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
